/-!
# Fixed P506/L0 second-sweep matter temporal regularity

The literal U5 current already generated by the complete joint action has the
local primitive regularity needed by the second full-occurrence matter leg at
every zero-slice occurrence.  Instantiating the local Cartan-restart theorem
therefore proves the second-sweep matter correction continuous in the full
recentered carrier.

No residual, target velocity, regularity receipt, branch, or free coefficient
enters the writer or this acceptance proof.
-/

